module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**stale claim survives its own correct edit** (INVALID STATE: a prose claim that was TRUE when written and became false through a CORRECT edit made elsewhere -- the deletion of a CI job, the removal of a symbol, a rename, a withdrawn change, or the closing of a referenced node -- while nothing in the citing artifact changed at the moment it became false. ",

    "HARM: it is invisible to every mechanism we have. Both halves were individually correct when authored, so no test, lint, type check or review of either diff can see the contradiction; the defect is CREATED BY THE CORRECT EDIT and therefore does not appear in that edit's diff. A fluent, well-reasoned wrong claim survives on readability -- one specimen below passed four review rounds. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, and the reason this is one class rather than four: the mechanism is identical -- a claim whose PREMISE is elsewhere, with no link from the premise back to the claim -- and only the severity differs. FOUR TIERS, each with a measured specimen. (i) MISDESCRIBES CANDIDATE EVIDENCE: `v1.compiler.compiler_tests_rust` `ct_evaluation_budget_consequence_falsifier_test` justified an opt-in arm by saying the --lib suite runs on every push; it wastes a reader's time. (ii) CONFERS STANDING IT DOES NOT HAVE: the same file's block above `emit_entry_point_absent_main_rs` announced itself as a WALL 'ENROLLED WHERE IT ACTUALLY EXECUTES', riding a required `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib` step -- and `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` contains ZERO occurrences of `cargo test`, the job having been deleted by the 2026-09-04 runner-capacity ruling under declared drop `rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path`. That is DESIGN 4b(1) RUNG INFLATION, and it is worse than (i) because an inflated wall means the class never ranks for climbing: everyone believes it is already held. (iii) THE REASONING ITSELF INVERTS WHILE THE WORDS STAY CORRECT-LOOKING: that same block rejected a wet transport because it 'would have been an inert lens asserting a safety property nothing runs', and the home it chose instead became exactly that. Not one word had to change for the argument's conclusion to reverse. (iv) THE REFERENT'S LIFECYCLE ENDS: a citation naming something that can be CLOSED -- a work item, a session, a node -- dies silently when that lifecycle ends. `test.claim.phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness` named `node://adhoc-da8c65c0-b3b` as the owner of a next-rung trigger; that node reached DONE without the capability it owed existing, so the trigger was retirable by nobody. The repair repointed it to `node://adhoc-f044ad97-222` -- THE AUTHORING LANE'S OWN WORK ITEM, which closes when that lane finishes. The same defect with a longer fuse, authored by the change that diagnosed the class, ratified through three review rounds, and caught only by a dashboard completion notice. ",

    "THE TELL THAT DISTINGUISHES (iv) FROM A HEALTHY CITATION IS ONE QUESTION, and it is decidable: if every session running today archived tonight, would this citation still have a referent tomorrow? A work item fails it by construction, and so does the manager session above it. Checking that a candidate node is currently `in_progress` answers the STATUS question and never the LIFETIME question -- which is precisely the check on which the defective repoint was ratified. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable. The population is discovered by sweeping prose for the dead premise and reading every hit in context, which is manual and has no denominator. ",

    "CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and NOT higher, because the general form is undecidable -- 'this sentence is still true' is not a property of the source. What IS decidable is the two structured sub-cases, and the ceiling is stated per sub-case rather than for the class: a citation naming a DECLARED SYMBOL is already checked by the parse-phase `v1_compiler.declaration_index` route in `v1_compiler.bin.claim_executor`, and a citation naming a LIFECYCLE-BOUNDED REFERENT is decidable the same way if such referents are modeled rather than spelled into a `String`. Free prose asserting a fact about CI shape is not reachable by either and stays at mitigation. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, naming the CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a typed citation carrier for lifecycle-bounded referents, such that a work-item or session identity CANNOT be written into a field whose contract is 'accountable owner of an outstanding obligation' -- sufficient that no `Accepted` program names a closable referent as the owner of a next-rung trigger. Until that exists the honest arm is the one taken here: name a STANDING AUTHORITY that owns the capability rather than any node. A grep, a sweep, or a one-off repair of the known instances does NOT fire this trigger; they are mitigation of a population, not prevention of the state. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when prose asserts a fact whose subject lives in ANOTHER file -- a CI job, a symbol, a step, a node, a rung -- ask what would have to change elsewhere for the sentence to become false, and whether anything would edit this file when it did. If the answer is 'nothing', the sentence is a candidate instance whether or not it is currently true. The corollary for authors: after any edit that DELETES or WITHDRAWS something, grep for the announcement of it, because the announcement is in a diff you are not looking at. ",

    "MEASUREMENT HAZARD, recorded because it cost six detector failures across two sessions on 2026-09-05: every sweep for this class returned a CONFIDENT CLEAN ANSWER for the rows it could not see. `grep -c` counts lines and misses phrases wrapping across emitted string literals (2 where the truth was 4); a normaliser stripping `///` but not `//` leaves a comment marker mid-phrase; an exact sentence misses a shorter variant; backticks around an identifier defeat a word-boundary match; and enumerating by premise returns files that correctly RECORD the deletion alongside files that assert it. A record QUOTING a false claim inside its own errata is not asserting it, and no regex separates quotation from assertion. Strip both comment forms and backticks, collapse whitespace, always run a control that MUST hit, and read every hit in context. ",

    "SCOPE NOT CLAIMED: the four tiers were measured on one lane's sweep of one premise. No claim is made that the tiers are exhaustive, nor that the population outside `v1.compiler.compiler_tests_rust`, `gunbc.emitted_closure_compile_seed_growth` and `test.claim.phantom_marker_type_argument_identity_witness` has been enumerated.) ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
